.content.content--en
	.content__sec.scroll-to-sec
		.my-container
			h2.content__title  specialisation
			p.content__text  Since 2006, we have been providing legal assistance to Russian and global corporations, state-owned entities, private clients and not-for-profit organisations. Our key competences are to support complex investment projects and deals, and resolve complicated disputes, including cross-border and international ones.
			br
			p.content__text  We combine high proficiency in law with skills in providing legal protection to corporations before Russian public authorities and have unrivalled experience of managing large-scale, multi-jurisdictional projects.
	.content__sec-colored
		.content__sec.scroll-to-sec
			.my-container
				h2.content__title  people
				p.content__text  Our clients’ interests are protected by nearly 100 attorneys and lawyers based at our offices in Moscow and St Petersburg.
		.content__sec.scroll-to-sec
			.my-container
				h2.content__title  expertise
				p.content__text  Our service covers all key fields of law. We are particularly strong in areas of work that are important to large corporations:
				br
				ul.content__list 
					li.content__item corporate/M&A
					li.content__item energy & natural resources
					li.content__item infrastructure/PPP construction
					li.content__item arbitration, litigation, insolvency
					li.content__item banking & finance
					li.content__item regulatory & compliance
					li.content__item tax & customs
					li.content__item real estate & investment
					li.content__item data protection and privacy
					li.content__item employment
		.content__sec.scroll-to-sec
		.my-container
			h2.content__title  scale
			p.content__text  Ivanyan and Partners is one of the Top-10* biggest and most successful law firms in Russia. Over the past five years (2020-2024), we have advised on projects worth $110 bn+ in aggregate and our work now extends to 54 countries on five continents.
			p.content__text-small  *as per the research conducted by the leading national legal market observer Pravo-300 for 2020-2024.
	.content__sec-lines.scroll-to-sec
		.my-container
			.content__subsec
				h2.content__title  selected experience
				h3.content__subtitle  corporate/M&A
				p.content__text  Advised a Chinese real property major on envisaged acquisition of a controlling stake in a Russian company with a big portfolio of Moscow commercial real estate. Deal value: $650 m+
				p.content__text  Advised the shareholders in Sibur Holding, Russia’s gas-processing and petrochemicals major, on sale of a 10% minority stake to China Petroleum & Chemical Corporation (Sinopec). Stake value: $1.34 bn
				p.content__text  Advised the shareholders in Sibur Holding on sale of 10% of the shares to the Chinese Silk Road Fund. Deal value: undisclosed
				
				p.content__text  Advised a private Russian investment group on disposing of a 20% participatory interest in a Russian gas-producing company to a Chinese energy corporation, including structuring the deal and advising on regulatory issues. Deal value: $48 m
			.content__subsec
				h3.content__subtitle  banking & finance
				p.content__text  Advised Gazprombank, Sberbank and Otkritie bank on syndicated financing for a joint venture of the Sibur Holding, the biggest petrochemical company in Russia, and China Petroleum & Chemical Corporation (Sinopec), the world’s biggest petrochemical company, aiming construction of the Amur Gas and Chemical Complex in Russia’s Far East. Bridge-financing: $1.5 bn
				
				p.content__text  Advised a major Russian bank on all legal aspects of loan financing to a Hong-Kong exchange listed producer of iron ore concentrate in the context of a project for developing one of Russia’s biggest ore deposits. Deal value: $240 m
				
				p.content__text  Advising an international investment group as a borrower concerning several stages in the financing of a project in Uzbekistan for construction, overhaul and development of wells on oil and gas condensate fields. <span style="display:block; margin-top:15px;">Total project investment: </span><span style="display:block; margin-top:15px;">1st stage financing: $200 m, </span><span style="display:block; margin-top:15px;">2nd stage financing: €180 m</span>
				
				p.content__text  Advised the developer and operator of a port in Russia’s Far East on attracting syndicated loan financing from VEB.RF, a major Russian bank. Credit line: ₽34 bn ($340 m)
				
			.content__subsec
				h3.content__subtitle  regulatory
				
				p.content__text  Advised a Fortune-500, Chinese state-owned energy corporation on Russian regulatory aspects of planned acquisition of an Israeli engineering company. Deal value: $120 m+
				p.content__text  Advised a Chinese investor on all legal aspects of acquiring 100% of a Russian bank, including obtaining consent from the Bank of Russia and the Federal Antimonopoly Service
				p.content__text  Advised Otkritie Holding, a Top-5 Russian finance group, on the regulatory aspects of acquiring from the Russian oil & gas major Lukoil 100% in a company operating Russia’s 2nd biggest diamond mine. Deal value: $1.45 bn
				p.content__text  Advised Rockwell Capital investment fund on regulatory aspects of setting up, together with state development corporation VEB.RF, a joint timber-processing holding company, involving construction of an advanced wood-processing complex in Eastern Siberia. Matter value: ₽150 bn+ ($1,5 bn+)
				
			.content__subsec
				h3.content__subtitle  infrastructure / energy / construction
				p.content__text  Advised an international HKSE-listed gambling operator on investment in a construction and development project for a hotel-casino complex in the Primorye Gambling Zone in Russia’s Far East. Potential investment: up to $350 m
				
				p.content__text  Advised a Russian company on a large-scale construction investment project for a new coal terminal in the Far East, including drafting and negotiating a contract with a Chinese engineering supplier for supply and installation of key equipment. Investment: ₽37 bn+ ($370 m)
				
				p.content__text  Advising a private investor on a long-term project for increasing the capacity of the Gazli natural underground gas storage facility, the biggest in Uzbekistan. The project will help in increasing gas exports from Uzbekistan to China. Investment: up to $1 bn
				p.content__text  Advised a Russian heavy industry major as an equipment supplier for a large-scale construction project for a copper concentrating complex in Uzbekistan. Contract value: up to $5 bn
				
			.content__subsec
				h3.content__subtitle  international arbitration and domestic dispute resolution
				
				p.content__text  Representing an international investment fund in arbitration proceedings over protection of the client’s investment in an oilfield service group in Russia, as well as enforcement procedures. Recovery amount: approximately $50 m
				
				p.content__text  Represented UK investors, former shareholders in a Latvian bank, in a claim against the Republic of Latvia under a UK-Latvia BIT. Claimed amount: €70 m
				p.content__text  Represented a road construction company in a precedent-setting dispute with the Federal Antimonopoly Service of Russia (FAS) concerning use of a concession agreement model for construction of a toll road. Project value: ₽20 bn+ ($200 m)
				p.content__text  Represented a major Russian LNG producer in several potentially precedent-setting disputes over applying a ‘take-or-pay’ covenant under Russian law as part of a project for construction of a big oxygen station. Claimed amount: ₽1 bn+ ($10 m)
				<br><br><br>
				p.content__text-small  The transaction amount is calculated based on the average exchange rate for January 2023 and expressed in RMB: USD 1 = CNY 6.90; EUR 1 = CNY 7.43; RUB 1 = CNY 0.09
				

